# Phase B: Reliability Core and Benchmark Ladder (Gate 1)

Following the roadmap in [`.round2-roadmap/updatedone/Phase B — Reliability core and benchmark ladder.md`](file:///c:/Users/adity/OneDrive/Desktop/SIH26079-RII/.round2-roadmap/updatedone/Phase%20B%20%E2%80%94%20Reliability%20core%20and%20benchmark%20ladder.md) and Section 4 & 5 of the *Hazard-Specific Reliability Implementation Blueprint*, Phase B implements **Gate 1**: establishing the universal `ReliabilityState` contract, the evidence and provenance graph schemas, the Failure Memory episode builder & retrieval engine, and the standardized benchmark ladder with cycle-block bootstrap evaluation.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Universal Contract Invariant**: Every downstream hazard specialist (Precipitation, Cyclone, Monsoon, Western Disturbance, Heatwave, Wind in Phases D–H) will emit the unified `ReliabilityState` contract defined in this phase.
> - **Benchmark Ladder Protocol**: V3 is evaluated alongside simpler baselines (climatology, persistence, raw spread, logistic regression, compact statistical model) under identical temporal splits (2024-H2 test set) and cycle-block bootstrap confidence intervals.

